x265: set CMP0025 and CMP0054 to NEW for CMake 4.

CMake 4 removed the OLD behaviour of these policies and refuses to configure.
CMP0025 only affects Apple's compiler name; NEW CMP0054 is the long-standing
default.

Upstream-Status: Pending (not QNX-specific: CMake 4)

--- a/source/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/source/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -7,13 +7,15 @@
 endif()
 message(STATUS "cmake version ${CMAKE_VERSION}")
 if(POLICY CMP0025)
-    cmake_policy(SET CMP0025 OLD) # report Apple's Clang as just Clang
+    # CMake 4 removed OLD support for this policy; it only affects Apple builds.
+    cmake_policy(SET CMP0025 NEW) # report Apple's Clang as AppleClang
 endif()
 if(POLICY CMP0042)
     cmake_policy(SET CMP0042 NEW) # MACOSX_RPATH
 endif()
 if(POLICY CMP0054)
-    cmake_policy(SET CMP0054 OLD) # Only interpret if() arguments as variables or keywords when unquoted
+    # CMake 4 removed OLD support; NEW is the long-standing default behaviour.
+    cmake_policy(SET CMP0054 NEW) # only unquoted if() arguments are dereferenced
 endif()
 
 project (x265)
